<title>UK: INTERVIEW - L&amp;G rules out life acquisitions.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - L&amp;G rules out life acquisitions.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British insurer Legal and General Group Plc (L&amp;G) on Thursday ruled out acquistions in the drive to grow the company's UK life and pensions business.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't want to be diverted. Our strategy is not dependent on mergers and acquisitions. We don't want our efforts diverted by someone else's problems,&quot; L&amp;G chief executive David Prosser told Reuters.</p>
<p>Prosser was speaking after the group had reported a 15 percent rise in operating profits for 1996 to 291.4 million stg.</p>
</text>
